              "# CORRECTED-WRAPUP 1-China's 2018 growth slows to 28-year low, more stimulus seen\nBy Kevin Yao and Yawen Chen\n\nJanuary 21, 2019 5:38 AM UTC Updated ago\n\n- Summary\n\n- Weak investment weighing on economy after debt clampdown\n- U.S. tariffs, slowing global demand dent exports\n- Trade war further souring business, consumer sentiment\n- More policy easing, stimulus measures expected in form of\n\nconstruction spending, special loan programmes, tax cuts",
